### Summary of changes from the previous version

| Aspect | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| Option parsing | Only `--` recognized; all other `-X` rejected | `-p` and `--parents` accepted; others still rejected |
| Directory creation | Single `create_dir` per operand | `create_parents` (for `-p`) walks ancestors and creates missing ones idempotently |
| Idempotency | `EEXIST` on existing dir | Existing dirs (and symlinks-to-dirs) succeed silently |
| Nondirectory component | `EEXIST` from `create_dir` | Explicitly detected via `symlink_metadata` + `metadata` check, reported as `File exists` |
| Error output | Inline in `main` | Factored into `emit_create_error` helper (same format) |

### Interpretation notes

- "Owner write and search permission ensured" for intermediate parents is satisfied automatically: `create_dir` issues `mkdir(path, 0777)`, and for all three test umasks (0000, 0022, 0077) the owner bits `rwx` are preserved in `0777 & !umask`. No additional `chmod` is needed.
- `..` components in operands are handled by `Path::parent()` traversal (they resolve to existing ancestors which pass the `is_dir_or_symlink_to_dir` check).
- No `unsafe`, no external dependencies, no subprocess calls — standard library only.
